From 0817904444ec6953f8ac274dbe804a9adf187d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] camera: Core reads the storage and lever context and
 publishes the known limit

Why: The known-limits table (SustainedFps.hpp) has no input yet: the camera
does not know which storage the take goes to, how full it is, or which
aids and audio are on, and no screen can show what the table says. Core
already keeps these facts in different places (the media profile and the
media snapshot in the application, UI.conf, the camera's own settings).
Original Apertar publishes camera-derived values as flat scalar fields
that the camera fills when the state is read and when it sends a settings
event: a runtime field of CaptureSettings with a "Runtime" comment, set in
settings() and emitSettingsEventLocked (exposureCompensationAvailable,
Types.hpp:132 and CameraController.cpp:8570 and :8779@upstream-1.6.0;
conventions CAM-18).

What: ApertarCoreApp::refreshLadderContext builds a sustained::Context
(storage type from the media class, filesystem, fill, aids from UI.conf,
audio, clip split) and hands it to CameraController::setLadderContext,
which stores it and sends a settings event when a fact changes or the
card crosses 94 percent. It runs on a media change, when the card crosses
94 percent in the media watcher's poll, after a UI switch, after a preset
and after set_frames_per_folder. The camera adds TDN, phase lock, Log and
the board (a Pi 5 or CM5 is the measured one; a simulated camera stands
for it) and fills five new state fields in settings() and in each settings
event: limit_fps (what the running mode holds for a 30-minute take, a
step, 0 = none known), limit_short_fps, limit_basis (measured, derived,
probable, unconfirmed or sensor), limit_by (back end, encoder, drive,
sensor or TDN) and limit_why (one sentence). H.264, ProRes and stills have
no limits. whyText in the header builds the sentence and is pinned by the
host test. probedModeLocked is the probe lookup that fillRungExtrasLocked
had inline, moved out so the limit can read a mode's binning too. Nothing
changes behaviour: fps_max, the ladder and every old field are as before.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the host tests pass (the sentence
cases are new in sustained_fps_test). In --simulate: get_state and the
settings event carry the five fields, limit_why reads like the page's
examples, set_preview_tdn false changes limit_fps, and the smoke shapes
still match 1.6.0's. Needs the camera, on the owner's rig with the NVMe
card: get_state at 4K Clear HDR 16-bit shows limit_fps 20 and limit_basis
unconfirmed. Pull the card and mount the T7: the fields change and the
camera does not (fps, mode and fps_max stay).

